course: dictionary
lesson: 6225
title: Mixed: many kinds together
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mixed means made of different kinds put together. A bag of mixed nuts has many kinds of nuts in it, so you can read the word and the thing it describes to find its meaning.
explain: Mixed is also the past form of mix. The verb goes mix, mixes, mixed, mixing. When you see mixed with a verb, ask yourself: did someone stir, join or combine things? The word «mixed» tells you it already happened.
explain: Mixed can also describe feelings or situations. «Mixed feelings» means you feel two things at once. «A mixed bag» means partly good and partly bad, so the clues are in the words around it.
fact: Mixed means made of different kinds put together.
fact: Mixed is the past form of mix: mix, mixes, mixed, mixing.
fact: «Mixed feelings» means feeling happy and sad at the same time.
fact: «A mixed bag» means partly good and partly bad.
fact: In maths, a mixed number is a whole number and a fraction, like 2 1/2.
exercise: «A bag of mixed nuts» has what in it? | Empty space | Nothing but sweets | *Many kinds of nut put together | Only one kind of nut
exercise: Which word shows that mixing happened in the past? | *mixed | mixes | mix | mixing
exercise: What do mixed feelings mean? | *Happy and sad at the same time | Only sad | Hungry and tired | Only happy
test: «A mixed bag» means what? | *Partly good and partly bad | Empty and bare | Only good things | Very heavy
test: In maths, what is a mixed number like 2 1/2? | A number with no fractions | *A whole number and a fraction together | Two whole numbers side by side | A fraction only
exam: What is in a mixed team, as in «Mixed teams of grown-ups and children make games fairer»? | Only grown-ups | Only animals | Only children | *Grown-ups and children together
